# Build output IS committed: `npm run build` regenerates lib/, and git installs
# (`github:a285292107s/dsh-rabbit-model-picker`) receive the repository verbatim — they
# run no build step, so an uncommitted lib/ makes every such install fail with
# "failed to import" (no entry point). Keep lib/ in sync with src/ on every
# change to src/: run `npm test` (build + gates) and commit both together.
# Source maps stay out; they are large and resolve nothing for a git install.
lib/*.map

# Dev-only toolchain.
node_modules/

# Local browser-automation scratch from manual verification.
.playwright-cli/

# Design-iteration working files (tasteskill v2): probe scripts, notes and the
# before/after screenshots the pass looked at. The record that ships is
# DESIGN.md §5.24 plus the refreshed shots/ images; this folder is scratch.
.taste-skill/

# Scratch under shots/, never authored: the extracted sheet (`_extract-css.cjs`),
# the two HTML harnesses the row/trigger scripts render and then screenshot, and
# the one-off probes and pixel-diff images written beside them. All of it rebuilds
# from `src/` on demand, so committing it only adds weight to every git install.
# The surfaces a reviewer is meant to open are the plain and `accept-*` / `audit-*`
# shots; anything named `_…` is an intermediate.
shots/_*
